    "openQuestions": [
        "chi(T, salt) for PEG/water in 2-10 mM MgCl2 is NOT determined by this task. The adopted equation of state is non-virial by construction, so it yields neither A2 nor chi; and no source for the Mg2+ salting-out coefficient was found this iteration. What IS bounded: 10 mM of a divalent chloride shifts the theta temperature by O(0.1-1 K) out of 375 K, i.e. <= 0.7% of the reduced temperature, which is far below the +/- 2% uncertainty on alpha. The bound is an argument, not a citation. Raised as task P-6.",
        "the crossover index alpha was fitted to LINEAR PEG. A PS->PEG reinitiation block copolymer (§3) is not the material it was fitted to.",
        "the 10-16 nm height range for dense PEG 5 kDa brushes, cited by C-0001, remains untraced. It is not used by anything and should be dropped rather than sourced."
